scenario description is, as stated in the source description:
    actions_of_rules expects answers ["description 1 produces item 1 action", "description 2 produces item 2 action", "description 3 produces item 3 action", "description 4 produces action 1", "description 4 produces item 4 action", "description 5 produces action 2", "description 5 produces item 5 action", "description 6 produces action 3", "description 6 produces action 4", "description 6 produces action 5", "description 6 produces action 6", "description 6 produces item 6 action"].
    actions_of_agents expects answers ["concerned data subjects acts as addressee in item 1 action", "conformity assessment bodies acts as addressee in item 3 action", "european commission acts as addressee in item 2 action", "european commission acts as addressee in item 5 action", "european commission acts as addresser in action 2", "general public acts as addressee in action 2", "market surveillance authorities acts as addressee in item 6 action", "market surveillance authorities acts as addresser in action 5", "market surveillance authorities public authoritiesbodies acts as addressee in action 6", "market surveillance authorities public authoritiesbodies acts as addresser in action 6", "market surveillance authority acts as addressee in action 3", "market surveillance authority acts as addresser in action 4", "national competent authorities acts as addressee in item 2 action", "national public authorities bodies supervise enforce the respect of acts as addressee in action 4", "national public authorities bodies supervise enforce the respect of acts as addresser in action 3", "national public authoritiesbodies superviseenforce eu law obligations protecting fundamental acts as addressee in item 6 action", "notified bodies acts as addressee in item 2 action", "notified bodies acts as addressee in item 4 action", "notified bodies designated under union harmonisation legislation listed in acts as addresser in action 1", "notifying authorities acts as addressee in item 3 action", "notifying authority acts as addressee in item 4 action", "notifying authority designated in accordance with union harmonisation legislation acts as addressee in action 1", "providers deployers of ai systems acts as addressee in action 5", "providers deployers of ai systems ai models acts as addressee in item 1 action", "providers of high risk ai systems including smcs smes acts as addressee in item 2 action", "providersdeployers of ai systems acts as addressee in item 6 action"].

query parts is:
    which thing is part of the description.

query kinds is:
    which thing is of the kind which kind.

query bearer is:
    the bearer role is which role.

query rules_of_act is:
    which rule is established by the act which act.

query provisions is:
    which thing is established in which provision.

query places is:
    which rule is laid down in which place.

query joint_rules is:
    which rule is established in more than one provision.

query prescriptive is:
    which thing is a prescriptive rule.

query constitutive is:
    which thing is a constitutive rule.

query triggers is:
    which thing is triggered by which event.

query actions_of_rules is:
    which rule produces which action.

query addressers is:
    which agent acts as addresser in which action.

query addressees is:
    which agent acts as addressee in which action.

query beneficiaries is:
    which agent acts as beneficiary in which action.

query actions_of_agents is:
    which agent acts as which role in which action.

query concerned_agents is:
    which rule concerns which agent.

query deadlines is:
    which thing has which temporal specification as deadline.

query starting_points is:
    which thing has which temporal specification as starting point.

query validity is:
    which thing has which temporal specification as validity.

query first_dates is:
    the first date of which temporal specification is which date.

query last_dates is:
    the last date of which temporal specification is which date.

query later_times is:
    which temporal specification is later than which second temporal specification.

query times_within is:
    which temporal specification is during which second temporal specification.

query broken_links is:
    which temporal specification breaks its link with which second temporal specification.

query due_dates is:
    which agent has which action due on which date.

query due_in_2027 is:
    which agent has which action due on which date in the period from 2027-01-01 to 2027-12-31.

query rules_without_conditions is:
    which rule has no written conditions.

query applies is:
    which rule applies to which party.

query must_perform is:
    which party must perform which action by which date under which rule.

query results is:
    which action has the result which result.

query datasets_of_results is:
    which dataset holds which result.

query digital_dimensions is:
    which rule has the digital dimension which dimension.

query processes is:
    which rule involves the process which process.

query datasets is:
    which thing is a dataset.

query standards is:
    which thing conforms to which standard.

query public_services is:
    which thing is a public service.

query references is:
    which rule references which resource.

query texts is:
    which thing is described by the text which text.

query other_values is:
    which thing has for which property the value which value.

query addresses is:
    which thing is identified by which address.

query plain_texts is:
    the texts of which property have no language.

